-------Scope-------
    Scope: Is the region of a computer program where name binding is valid. Scopes can vary in range, from small loops to as much as an entire application.
    Name Binding: An association of a name to an entity, such as a variable.
    1. Global Scope: A class, variable/value/function in the global scope that can be used anywhere in the entire program, extends Node (Node is globally accessible).
    2. Function Scope: A variable/value that is only visible inside the function (params and var declarations).
    3. Code Block Scope: A variable/value that is only visible inside code blocks, such as an if statement, match statement, for & while loops, etc.
